  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "none",
    "relation": "uses_without_test",
    "tranche": "T4",
    "tranche_reason": "It evaluates alternative edge-selection procedures and circuit-faithfulness metrics on GPT-2 IOI, testing part of the evaluation-sensitivity claim with a different circuit-construction setup. It does not test the original head circuit itself.",
    "gate_note": "The study reports MIB faithfulness metrics for GPT-2 IOI circuits built with different edge-selection methods and hyperparameters. These results bear on V5's metric and selection sensitivity. It does not test whether the original 26-head circuit has the stated roles, whether other methods recover the same circuit, or whether the mechanism transfers across models or prompt variants. Other task results and the cited original IOI findings are not recorded as rows.",
    "test_reason": "The study uses GPT-2 IOI as one MIB benchmark task to score its own edge-selection methods (ILP, bootstrapping, PNR) against the greedy baseline. All IOI numbers are the study's own method compared with a baseline. It never examines the Wang et al. head circuit, its head classes, backup heads, transfer, prompt variants or overlap with other methods. It also never varies ablation type, metric definition or prompt distribution to show how faithful a fixed IOI circuit looks. Different selection methods yielding different CMD/CPR scores is a methods-performance result, not a test of V5's evaluation-sensitivity claim.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Largely correct. The authors conclude that principled edge selection (bootstrapping, PNR, ILP) yields more faithful circuits than greedy selection across most MIB tasks and models. ILP gives only modest faithfulness gains and scales poorly. The best PNR needs per-model-task tuning. Higher total edge scores from ILP not translating into faithfulness suggests a gap between attribution scores and true edge importance.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "Uses EAP-IG edge scores and compares greedy selection with ILP, bootstrapping and positive-negative-ratio selection; it does not reproduce the original study's head-level IOI circuit analysis.",
    "method_sensitivity": "For GPT-2 IOI, reported CMD and CPR outcomes vary across selection methods; CMD also varies across PNR values, and CPR varies across bootstrap iteration counts.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "In GPT-2 IOI, 9.1% of edges get EAP-IG scores of both signs across 10 data samples.",
        "proposed_claim": "Edge attribution scores for IOI circuit discovery are sign-unstable across data resamples for a notable fraction of edges.",
        "row_ids": []
      },
      {
        "finding": "MIB faithfulness scores for GPT-2 IOI circuits shift with the edge-selection procedure (greedy, ILP, bootstrapping, PNR) given fixed EAP-IG scores.",
        "proposed_claim": "Discovered IOI circuit faithfulness depends on the subgraph-selection algorithm, not only on the scoring method.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r5",
